WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.890
Rain clouds settle over a
fell in the Lake District,

2
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.210
in England's north-west.

3
00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.010
Far to the south-east,
in a drought summer,

4
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:10.170
a reservoir shrinks.

5
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:16.110
England had droughts
in 2022, 2025 and 2026.

6
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.670
At home, each person uses about
137 litres of water a day.

7
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.750
In Germany, 120 to 123.

8
00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:28.490
So why is it the
south-east that runs short?

9
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.190
Does its rain all evaporate?

10
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.730
Can't the pipes from the north reach it?

11
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.550
In this mission, you'll follow water
from the reservoir to your tap,

12
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.410
and on to the river.

13
00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.790
Then you'll see why the gap between supply
and demand changes with the seasons.

14
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:49.090
Your mission: find out why the south-east
is the part of Britain running short

15
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:49.950
of water.
